# default mode, which is what `python3 -m tools.company_network_isolation` prints.
# R15-proven both ways in tests/tools/test_company_network_isolation.py (7 tests, synthetic
# trees with known answers, including one asserting the control can PASS).
python3 -m tools.company_network_isolation --gate || exit 1

# ── GATE 11: a file_scope may not name ground a generator rewrites ──────────────────────────
# THE CLASS FIX (R10) for the eight-day starvation of G13_projection_consumers, 2026-08-19.
# G13 sat at stage `build`, unblocked, dependency satisfied, and was never drawn -- because its
# `file_scope` named `site/data/`, the PUBLISHER'S OUTPUT directory. That directory is rewritten
# every cycle, so it permanently carries uncommitted changes; `supervisor._unmerged_work_paths`
# reported that correctly and the BUILD draw deprioritised the atom on every single tick, in
# silence. Measured the same day on the real draw: 22 of 27 buildable atoms deprioritised,
# leaving FIVE. That is the mechanism behind the level-move collapse of 08-15..08-18.
#
# NOT A PURITY RULE ABOUT OUTPUTS, and the refusal message says so. An atom that owns a
# generator has a real argument for declaring what it writes; the objection is the CONSEQUENCE
# -- the declaration makes the atom permanently invisible to its own build lane and nothing
# reports it. The gate names the starvation and the repair, not a convention.
#
# The oracle is DERIVED, not declared: an AST pass reads the generators themselves rather than
# trusting a hand-kept list of directories (116 artefacts found by segment-join; a full-path
# literal search finds only 17, because generators build paths as PROJECT / "site" / "data" / x).
# RATCHET both ways -- 11 known declarations frozen, a NEW one fails, a REPAIRED one also fails
# so the freeze can only shrink. R15-proven in tests/tools/test_file_scope_generated_paths.py
# (18 tests), including both fail-closed paths: an oracle that finds nothing must RAISE, never
# report a clean tree.
python3 -m tools.file_scope_generated_paths || exit 1

# ── GATE 12: a report is a RENDERING; production code may not import it ─────────────────────
# Director instruction, 2026-08-19, narrowed on the strength of the measurement: "Fix the one
# real production violation and make it impossible for new importers to appear. Leave the 77
# test files reaching into renderer internals alone for now -- that's a rebuild, not a
# decoupling, and the cost is out of proportion to the harm."
#
# The one violation was tools/generate_dashboard_data.py::extract_regulatory importing
# `populate_compliance_scorecard` from the 9,838-line report. That function's own docstring
# admitted the coupling in writing, so the renderer had become the HOME of a computation two
# surfaces needed. It now lives in saas/reporting/compliance_scorecard_population.py and both
# surfaces import it there, which is why this gate can be frozen at ZERO rather than at one.
#
# DELIBERATELY ASYMMETRIC, and the asymmetry IS the instruction: production importers are
# frozen at zero and a new one FAILS; test importers are counted and published as debt in
# docs/design/ANNUAL_REPORT_IMPORT_DEBT.md and NEVER enforced. A frozen test count would fail
# on every legitimate edit to a report test -- a gate that punishes ordinary work and gets
# disabled within a week, while arguing with the instruction that created it.
# R15-proven in tests/tools/test_annual_report_import_ratchet.py, including the fail-closed
# path: a scan that reads nothing must RAISE, never report clean layering it never looked at.
python3 -m tools.annual_report_import_ratchet || exit 1

# ── GATE 13: the half-hourly spine is the market, not an implementation detail ──────────────
# Director ruling, 2026-08-24: "GB settlement is half-hourly and that is not an implementation
# detail, it is the market. So the half-hourly spine stays half-hourly. Aggregate in the
# reporting and ledger layers if that's where the memory goes, but the settlement and metering
# record keeps its grain. And put a control on it that fails if anything half-hourly-dependent
# is added while the fold is live, so this can't be discovered later by a tariff that silently
